# animations.vn - every animation feature, one after another: move transforms and easing, the animate presets,
# loops, keyframe animations from rig.json, and a layered character that idles, talks and blinks by itself.
# Nothing jumps here: put the cursor on the `label animation_showcase:` line and use Preview from cursor (Ctrl+Enter).
# Characters: alice (park.vn, a flat image: presets and transforms) and mina (mina.vn, layered: also her rig.json).

label animation_showcase:
  scene bg_park_evening fade 0.5
  show alice neutral at 0.25 fade 0.4
  show mina at 0.75 fade 0.4
  "Animation tour. Alice is a flat image, Mina is a layered character with a rig.json." #trnr
  mina: Look at me before anything has been said: I breathe, and now and then I blink. That is rig.json "idle" and "blink". #g2bo

  # --- 1. move: position, size, tilt, lift, opacity and mirroring, tweened together ---
  "1. move: y= scale= rot= alpha= flip= tween together with the position, with an ease." #kglp
  alice: Slide, with three different easings. #v6ag
  move alice to center 0.6 ease=out
  move alice to left 0.6 ease=back
  move alice to 0.4 0.8 ease=bounce
  move alice to left 0.5 ease=elastic
  alice: Size, lift and tilt at once. #pzfi
  move alice scale=1.25 y=-0.04 rot=-6 0.5 ease=back
  move alice scale=1 y=0 rot=0 0.4
  alice: Fade out, turn around, come back. #n7nk
  move alice alpha=0.25 0.4
  move alice flip=on
  move alice alpha=1 0.4
  move alice flip=off

  # --- 2. animate presets: they add to where a character stands ---
  "2. animate <char> <name>: nine presets. One-shots wait for the end." #jo5z
  alice: nod #n7ym
  animate alice nod
  alice: bob #r0pc
  animate alice bob
  alice: bounce #k3lj
  animate alice bounce
  alice: hop #l2aq
  animate alice hop
  alice: pulse #zfnn
  animate alice pulse
  alice: shiver #dq7e
  animate alice shiver
  alice: shake #uwbe
  animate alice shake
  alice: sway #i1d6
  animate alice sway
  alice: breathe #vygv
  animate alice breathe
  alice: Seconds and strength change them: bounce again, 1.6 seconds and half again as high. #pqxk
  animate alice bounce 1.6 strength=1.5

  # --- 3. loops: they go on until stop, and survive a save or a rollback ---
  "3. loop: repeats until stop (or hide, or the next scene). A new loop replaces the old one." #q9f1
  animate alice sway loop
  alice: I am swaying. This lasts across lines. #lwym
  animate alice bob 0.8 loop strength=2
  alice: Now bobbing quickly, and that replaced the sway. #snj2
  animate alice pulse 1.4 loop
  alice: Pulsing. A one-shot adds to a loop, so watch. #ciig
  animate alice hop
  alice: Both at once. Now stop. #t5ge
  animate alice stop

  # --- 4. nowait: run animations side by side ---
  "4. nowait: start an animation and carry on, so several characters move together." #kase
  animate alice bounce 1.2 nowait
  animate mina hop nowait
  move alice to center 1.2 ease=inout nowait
  move mina scale=1.1 1.2 ease=inout
  move alice to left 0.5
  move mina scale=1 0.4

  # --- 5. keyframe animations from Mina's rig.json "animations" ---
  "5. rig.json animations: keyframes of your own. Mina has wave, giggle and head_tilt." #ah9s
  mina: wave #h8ne
  animate mina wave
  mina: giggle, looping #t7ov
  animate mina giggle loop
  mina: Still giggling, while I talk. A rig animation can also be stretched: animate mina wave 3. #rukz
  animate mina stop
  animate mina wave 3

  # --- 6. per-part animation: part= moves just that part, about its pivot ---
  "6. part=: one part of a layered character, about its pivot (rig.json \"pivots\")." #woaw
  mina: head_tilt is keyframes that move my face, bangs, eyes, mouth and hair together. #sn9t
  animate mina head_tilt
  mina: part= plays any animation on one part: my hair sways by itself. #pit0
  animate mina sway 2.5 loop part=hair_back strength=2
  mina: And my face nods, while the hair carries on. #juzh
  animate mina nod 0.6 part=face strength=3
  animate mina stop

  # --- 7. what a layered character does by itself ---
  "7. idle, speak and blink: nothing in the script asks for these." #odat
  mina: Watch my mouth while I talk, a longer sentence helps: it moves while the letters appear, and stops when the line is done. #k1la
  mina: Eyes closed on purpose: a slot set in the script wins over blinking. #w2b5
  show mina eyes=closed
  mina: And open again. #wekj
  show mina eyes=open

  # --- 8. wind: the scene's wind pushes every physics chain (rig.json "physics") ---
  "8. wind: it pushes every physics chain of a rig.json, here my hair. It lasts until wind off or the next scene." #cee5
  wind right 0.6 gusts=0.4 1.5
  mina: A breeze from the left. My hair streams out to the right and picks up the gusts. #ivqi
  wind left 0.9 gusts=0.8 1
  mina: And now a strong one from the other side. #xiqt
  wind off 2
  mina: Calm again. A chain's windScale sets how much of the wind it feels: 0 ignores it, a negative number mirrors it. #ldu8

  # --- the end ---
  "That is all of them. Reduce motion (Options) turns the loops, shakes and hops off." #feof
  menu:
    "Once more." #as01:
      jump animation_showcase
    "Done." #as02:
      hide alice fade 0.4
      hide mina fade 0.4
      end
